      "Corrected a record that had been false for about ten hours before anyone read it. Pull request 19 was merged by the owner at 2026-09-15T09:29:12Z from head 802f520, and this file plus the release status had been asserting it was unmerged and that learning scope stayed blocked from main. Main is 8162707 and carries development through 802f520 - the scope pre-registration - and nothing later, so the harness replacement, the Java declaration, CONSTITUTION.md and the completion fix are all still development-only. Promotion was the owner own action; no agent authorizes it.",
      "The Java experiment is confirmed to have executed, from the run log rather than by inference. Hosted run 35062707190 prints active knowledge v3, candidate extracted-46e181f05a9c6f5dab5b9c21be5f07f3, claim \"Any class can have more than one constructor.\", boundary \"Java classes compiled and executed by OpenJDK 21, whose constructors differ in parameter list\". The candidate is an extracted corpus candidate, harnessesForDeclaration has no default pair, and its experiment throws CRU-0050 unless the fixture assertions pass with the executed negative control failing - so javac and java ran on the runner and the claim verified inside the declared boundary.",
      "Every active knowledge version is now marked corpus-backed or NOT corpus-backed, reusing the one discriminator a fixture cannot forge - membership in the restored corpus - factored per version as corpusBackedVersions rather than reinvented. hasRealCorpusKnowledge asks whether the store holds any real knowledge, and one real version answers yes for the whole store, which is why it could not surface the version the deleted harness had left behind. Covered by test/realCorpusLearning.test.js.",
      "Council egress exists as one dispatch-only workflow, authorized by the owner on 2026-09-16 and bounded by assertions rather than by its own comments. .github/workflows/council-consult.yml has no schedule and no push trigger, so egress happens when a person asks and at no other time; permissions are contents: read; the prompt travels through the environment rather than being interpolated into the shell, because an inline ${{ inputs.prompt }} is substituted before bash parses the line and free-form text is the point of the input; the consult is redirected rather than piped, because a pipeline reports tee status and a CRU-0034 refusal would otherwise have read as a green job. The deliberation is retained as an artifact and written into no governed record: it marks no gate and authorizes no promotion.",
      "Crucible free-only is enforced rather than incidental. createConfiguredAdapters builds an adapter for every provider whose credential is in the environment, so before this one paid key reaching one job would have spent the owner money with nothing in the run saying so. The registry now carries a billing tier per provider and consult drops paid adapters before distribution, reporting each exclusion because not consulted and not available are different facts. Perplexity is marked paid deliberately: a Perplexity Pro subscription does not cover the API billing this adapter uses, and assuming it did already cost this repository a blocked gate.",
      "R8 was unsatisfiable by construction, and the reason was never the corpus. proveInjection required a source recorded quarantined whose stored content still carried the patterns, but SafeInformationRetriever returns content null on injection signals and the worker then records the refusal without ever writing a durablePath - blocker: retrieved content was quarantined before persistence - so the prover skipped every document the safeguard caught before testing it. proveExecutable was further off: the retriever does not record a quarantine for executable bytes at all, it throws at the magic-byte check, and the worker catches that into retrieval-blocked with the sentence in blocker, so neither half of what that prover required is ever written. Both now read the recorded refusal with content absent, which is what the safeguard did, while the admitted-document guard is unchanged: bytes present means the screen did not stop them. Established by driving the real SourceRetrievalWorker in test/sourceRetrievalWorker.test.js, and both branches shown load-bearing by disabling each in turn.",
      "The gate-evidence fingerprint proved itself in production at run 35067259424: it dropped the inherited R8 outcome to unproven because realCorpusSafety.js, one of R8 deciders, had changed. An inherited proof did not survive the code that produced it, which is exactly what that mechanism was built for and the first time it has fired on a real change.",
      "The prompt-injection refusal was never missing, only unread. Oversight publishes encrypted-custody-report.json in plaintext beside the ciphertext, and its sourceReviews record 25 quarantines among 406 decisions - 24 policy refusals and exactly one \"prompt-injection content\", linked-source:5ab0eabad5e6714491c75fabab25d6afdf54218c4bdbfe705592c08de4baef62. Crucible queue does not carry Oversight reason, so that source arrives as oversight-vetting-pending and the prover, reading queue state, correctly saw no quarantine. The hosted job had been cloning that file all along to join the ciphertext parts. It is read now, two fields only, as candidate evidence from an independent party rather than as instruction, and credited only alongside the corpus not holding the refused bytes - the report is plaintext, so membership of the vetted repository is its only trust basis and the content check is what makes that sufficient.",
      "The content-absence half of the oversight refusal check is load-bearing in production, not only under test. Run 35068425740 read the report, found the single prompt-injection quarantine, and refused to credit it because the corpus stores that content hash - and no other review shares it, so the bytes are there because they were published, not because a duplicate shares a file. Crediting the decision field alone would have marked R8 prompt-injection satisfied on a refusal that kept nothing out.",
      "Refused content no longer reaches learning. Every source whose contentSha256 appears in a quarantined review is dropped on consumption, each exclusion logged, and the log states plainly that this closes the exposure without making the upstream refusal evidence that it held. All 25 rather than only the injection one, because the 24 policy refusals are provenance refusals - classifySource rejects non-HTTPS, denied hosts, .onion, private addresses and credentials in the URL - and corroboration requires two independent identified sources, so a provenance-refused source can never contribute one. Mining them would have added records that could never be used.",
      "Confirmed and enforced permanent repair-evidence retention plus a full 365-day Devlog-Pruned archive floor.",
      "Repaired CRU-0013 test-fixture drift by replacing the obsolete personal GitHub noreply fixture with the repository-configured 6076446993 noreply identity; the privacy detector and allow rules were not weakened.",
      "Fresh hosted verification rejected the first CRU-0013 repair because the unit test uses a synthetic GitHub identity; corrected the fixture to derive the noreply address from config.privacy.githubIdentity so no personal address is embedded and the identity contract remains testable."
    ],
    "verification": [
      "npm run test:all 863/863 at this change. The count rose by one with the evaluateR2 regression test, which was shown failing against the previous implementation before the repair existed.",
      "validate, docs:check, lint:workflows, audit:clutter, audit:privacy, audit:security, audit:ai-conflict-governance, audit:governance, audit:design-brief, audit:core-ref, audit:failure-codes, audit:circulation, audit:coordination and git diff --check all exit 0.",
      "Hosted at 259cf60: eighteen of eighteen Self-Test legs green, CodeQL and both Analyze jobs green, both AI handoff policy and AI conflict governance runs green, both locked-PR guards, monitor sync and the DEVLOG archive job green.",
      "Prove R4-R8 was read rather than assumed and has changed. Custody now verifies oversight-vetted with queue hash 54a976c3c02c1cbeaa522ccece1053a8e3516885de56cd006541a809d1c915ef over 403 stored source files, 8 documents and 526 links; the job reaches corroboration and uploads three artifact files. 25,981 usable candidates from 297 sources; one claim corroborated by two independent sources (\"Any class can have more than one constructor.\"); independent-source counts 1 at 0.8, 1 at the configured 0.74, 2 at 0.7, 10 at 0.6, 34 at 0.5. It fails closed on CRU-0026, not CRU-0023. No gate advanced and none was marked passed.",
      "Fill the candidate URL holding queue is green. It no longer fails closed on an empty NVIDIA_NIM_MODEL: the model is pinned in the workflow and run 34949648646 printed it unmasked as nvidia/nemotron-3-nano-30b-a3b. That run searched 0 topics because all 16 recorded a blocked run at 2026-09-15T08:32:29Z and a blocked topic consumes its daily slot, so a green check here is not evidence that R3 admitted anything and evaluateR3 still reads pending.",
      "npm run test:all 873/873 at this change, with the two new rules shown failing under mutation first. The failure-code ratchet holds at 581 uncoded throw sites and none added; the fly-by-wire ratchet holds at 57 direct edges and none added, with scopePreRegistration placed in the learning organ.",
      "npm run test:all 879/879 at this change, 873 before it. The failure-code ratchet holds at 581 uncoded throw sites with none added and the fly-by-wire ratchet at 57 direct edges with none added, with durableGateEvidence placed in the learning organ. test/workflow.test.js is 32/32 with its cache assertions moved onto the replacement mechanism rather than dropped.",
      "npm run test:all 881/881, from 879. Both previously surviving mutations were re-applied after the tests existed and are now killed. The known-bug ledger picked up one entry for test/soakRun.test.js during the soakGate mutation run; it was verified as an induced failure, confirmed passing at this tip, and reverted rather than committed as a real open bug.",
      "npm run test:all 888/888 at this change. Failure-code ratchet 581 uncoded with none added; fly-by-wire 57 direct edges with none added. test/hostedExperimentHarnesses.test.js registered in both testCadenceCoreLegacy and _testCadenceCore.",
      "Added regression coverage for exact one-year archive retention and for preserving an earlier repair observation when later evidence is recorded.",
      "Hosted run 37034597883 identified CRU-0013 at test/privacy.test.js:20; the repair changes only that obsolete allowed-identity fixture and retains CRU-0006 as an external Administration-read credential blocker.",
      "Fresh Self-Test run 37036574698 proved the first privacy correction incomplete: audit source sanitation no longer drove the failure, but test/privacy.test.js assertion failed. The follow-up derives the technical noreply fixture from the test configuration instead of hard-coding any account identity."
    ],
    "remaining": [
      "Do not weaken handoff, coordination, learning-custody, collision, security, or promotion gates to obtain green cosmetics, and never mark a gate passed on a run that was refused before it started or that exited before emitting a verdict.",
      "Resolved 2026-09-16: the corpus arithmetic difference was a phantom. The custody report counts content-addressed stored files and intakePathways counts sources without content, so sources minus files is the number of sources sharing a file, never the number without content. 534 sources, 128 without content, 406 with content held in 403 files, 3 sharing. The corpus summary now reports sourcesWithContent beside documentsWithContent and a regression test pins both readings.",
      "Second half of the owner's combined choice, in the Vetting-and-Governance-oversite. repository and not this one: have Oversight carry a copy of the gate evidence into independent custody. Crucible now emits gate-evidence.json inside its retained artifact, which is the input that half consumes. Oversight already pushes and is the independent party, so the evidence ends up in custody Crucible does not control - which is the point of splitting it this way.",
      "R8 is the only gate reporting pending on the real corpus, and both reasons are named. The prompt-injection safeguard is not firing: 60 documents carry those patterns and none is recorded as quarantined, which is the safeguard not having fired rather than evidence that it did. And no document in the restored corpus begins with executable magic bytes, so that behaviour cannot be demonstrated on this corpus at all - a fact about the corpus, not a gap to route around.",
      "R4-R7 stay reported rather than passed because the experiment behind them has run exactly once. A run that learns rather than restores is what repeats the measurement, and a restored store will keep short-circuiting that - so getting a second independent execution needs thought about how, not just another dispatch.",
      "Owner decision: whether to retract active knowledge v1, which the deleted hardcoded harness promoted and R5 still counts. It is reported on every run and no gate is marked passed while it is counted, but no agent retracts governed learning state on its own.",
